lar intratubular bodies</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><year>1965</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>1340</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4158483</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crew</surname><given-names>FAE</given-names></name><name><surname>Fell</surname><given-names>HB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The nature of certain ovum like bodies found in seminiferous tubules</article-title><source>Quart J Micro Sci</source><year>1992</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>557</fpage><lpage>79</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bradbury</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Bunge</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oocytes in seminiferous tubules</article-title><source>Fertil Steril</source><year>1958</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13501267</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vegni-Talluri</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bigliardi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Vanni</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Tota</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Testicular microliths: Their origin and structure</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1980</year><volume>124</volume><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6106071</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajpert-De Meyts</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Giwercman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The association of testicular carcinoma in situ with intratubular microcalcifications</article-title><source>J Urol Pathol</source><year>1994</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>42</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Halley</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The growth of sertoli cell tumours: A possible index of differential gonadotropic activity in the male</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1963</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>220</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14044198</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT19"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Janzen</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mathieson</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooperberg</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>delRio</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Golding</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Testicular microlithiasis: Sonographic and clinical features</article-title><source>AJR Am J Roentgenol</source><year>1992</year><volume>158</volume><fpage>1057</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1566667</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT20"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nistal</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez- Garcia</surname><given-names>C</g